@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
 The four-going-out from the presence is older than the chariots.
 The Spirit moved on the face of the waters at creation (Genesis 1:2), and the water tells the wind's story: __“a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into *four heads*”__ (Genesis 2:10) — one source at the presence, parted four ways to reach the whole earth, as the four spirits go forth from standing before the Lord.
 Wind above, water below — two carriers of one _ruach_, sent out fourfold at the beginning and gathering home from the same four corners at the end.
-And mark who waits at the corners: on the garment, the corner is where the law hangs its reminder — __“that ye may look upon it, and *remember all the commandments* of the LORD”__ (Numbers 15:39) — and at the earth's four wings wait __“the remnant… which *keep the commandments* of God”__ (Revelation 12:17).
+At the corners wait those who keep the commandments: on the garment, the corner is where the law hangs its reminder — __“that ye may look upon it, and *remember all the commandments* of the LORD”__ (Numbers 15:39) — and at the earth's four wings wait __“the remnant… which *keep the commandments* of God”__ (Revelation 12:17).
 The winds gather from the hem those who kept the hem.
 
